  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Tormach mill post remembers the last tool it loaded in this program.\nA consecutive request for that tool skips the pre-change retract, G30 and M6.\nThe first tool change remains unconditional.\nDifferent tools and a return to an earlier tool still change.\nEach section keeps G43, the machine-Z lift and the clearance before its first X/Y traverse.\n\n## Cause\n\nEvery TOOL record requested a full tool change.\nG30 could lower Z to the stored tool-change position before the next lift, even when the tool stayed the same.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `repeated_tool_skips_g30_and_m6_but_keeps_compensation_lift_and_clearance` failed before the fix and passes after it.\n- `a_different_tool_and_a_return_to_an_earlier_tool_each_change_again` failed before the fix and passes after it.\n- Restoring the upstream CPS killed both pins. Restoring the fixed CPS passed both pins. This checks the one new guard.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- The normal `microarc_test_part` suite passed both tests.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n`docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/microarc_test_part.nc` removes exactly three lines before the second T1 section: the pre-change `G53 G0 Z0`, `G30` and `T1 M6`.\nThe diff contains no other NC or CL changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nPathPilot Hub, a physical controller, Windows, macOS and the release gate were not exercised.\nThe post does not rely on PathPilot optimizing a same-tool M6.\nThe decision ledger records the public-document readings and rejected alternatives.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR touches the changed files.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Tormach skips redundant G30/M6 for consecutive sections using the same tool while preserving compensation and safe clearance.\n\nFixes #1626\n",
